      "worked": "The line $x-2y=4$ has gradient $\\dfrac12$, so the normal gradient is $\\dfrac12$ and the tangent gradient is $-2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2(2x+1)^{-1/2}\\\\y'&=-2(2x+1)^{-3/2}\\\\-2(2x+1)^{-3/2}&=-2\\\\(2x+1)^{3/2}&=1\\\\x&=0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt $x=0$, $y=2$. Hence,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-2&=\\dfrac12(x-0)\\\\y&=\\dfrac{x}{2}+2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
